\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20\lang1033 0.2 \tab}Fabrice Marguerie pointed out that real is suboptimal when used on a}
 intel platform; Real uses 6 bytes to represent a value, single uses 4 and double uses 8. Intel has native support for singles and doubles, but *not* for reals, it turns out. Therefore reals are much slower than singles.\line 
I replaced all reals with singles and the performance was boosted quite a lot more than I had expected. Thank you, Fabrice!{\lang1033 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20\lang1033 0.3 \tab}}Fixed some bugs, added some functionality. It\rquote s now possible to decide which rules are employed, and to visually get an idea of *when* the rules are fired.{\lang1033 
\par }}